  "note": "Code, legacy code, name key, description, rate, official return text, official deduction text and profile membership are taken mechanically from the official gross list (the code of the column Momskode NY). Package choices, not in the source: tax_type, accounts, EN 16931 category and VATEX code, evidence type, box mapping and signs, and the mapping of the official deduction text to deductible_pct, deduction_key and deduction_cap (spec 19, section 2). Sign convention: sign multiplies the posted signed amount (debit positive, credit negative) so that the normal case is positive in the box: output VAT and sales bases -1, input VAT and purchase bases +1 (F-DK-2, to confirm in 08). For a code without deduction or with the key of a reverse-charge pair the box mapping follows the official return text: a code with no deduction has no input VAT box (the counter line is a zero line). `profiles` are the business types 1 to 4 of the list (1 trade in DK only, 2 DK mixed, 3 also foreign trade, 4 mixed with foreign trade) and 5 for special codes. The apply input vat_profile (and include_special_codes) selects the codes. Not included, see CHANGELOG: special schemes (K620 to K650, S83 to S87), refund scheme (K710, K720), OSS (S61 to S65), local sales VAT abroad (S88). Tax classes tcl_goods and tcl_services come from EU_VAT",
